>
>
>
>     On Thursday, September 25, 2014 1:28:10 AM UTC-4, la gleki wrote:
>
>
>         TR NS, if you feel that it would work for you, invent this
>         cmavo and start using it!
>
>         It'd be also nice if you could define the syntax of this new
>         cmavo in PEG but we all believe that it wouldn't be ambiguous
>         syntactically so defining in PEG is not a must.
>
>         What doesn't work for others might work for you and then more
>         people.
>
>
>     As my skill improves, I imagine I will inevitable do so. But that
>     will take some time yet. In the mean time, what unused cmavo are
>     left that I could use?
>
> Probably you would want cmavo in CV'Vi space where C is a consonant=20
> and V is a vowel.
>
> Check if a given cmavo isnt defined yet here:
> e.g.
> http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/be'ei=20
> <http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/be%27ei>
> See? {be'ei} hasn't been yet defined.
> You may try others.
>

If what you want is forethought be...bei...be'o, I would suggest you to=20
use either { lo'oi <http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/lo%27oi>=20
[bridi+ke'a] (vau) } or { lo poi'i=20
<http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/poi%27i> [bridi+ke'a] (kei) }  (those=20
are equivalent in meaning; bridi+ke'a means "a bridi containing=20
=E2=80=94implicitly or explicitly=E2=80=94 a relative pronoun {ke'a}, just =
like the=20
bridi introduced by {noi} and {poi}").

As their word shape shows, {lo'oi}=20
<http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/lo%27oi> and {poi'i}=20
<http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/poi%27i> are experimental cmavo. The=20
former is just the full-bridi version of {lo} (and it belongs to an=20
experimental selma'o LOhOI):  lo broda be ko'a bei ko'e bei ko'i (be'o)=20
=3D lo'oi (ke'a) broda ko'a ko'e ko'i (vau).
This can be handy for building complex description sumti containing=20
several nesting levels, such as {lo'oi mi kucli lo du'u xu kau do penmi=20
ke'a} =3D "The one(s) which is/are such that I wonder whether you met=20
him/her/them".

As for {poi'i}, it belongs to the NU selma'o and has the following=20
definition: =C2=AB x1 is such that poi'i abstraction is true; x1 binds ke'a=
=20
within the abstraction. =C2=BB
Example: {mi poi'i do penmi ke'a (kei)} =3D {mi se penmi do}  (the ke'a=20
pronoun stands for the x1 of poi'i, here it's "mi").

Both {lo'oi} and {poi'i} are currently supported by the experimental=20
version of Camxes <http://ilmen.tk/lojban/camxes-exp.html> (this is an=20
unofficial version of Camxes used for testing various grammar change=20
proposals and implementing most of the frequently used experimental cmavo).

mi'e la .ilmen. mu'o

